I implemented the node from its declared signature and capabilities. I left out both operations requests, because each needs authority this node was not granted and that the build target cannot provide:

1. **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`** can't be done. The target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem import at all. Adding one would give the node authority its graph type (`with StateHandle<'seen', read>`) doesn't declare.
2. **Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=…`** would mean importing `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`. This node only holds `state-read`, so adding the import would quietly widen its authority past what the graph and validator approved. It would also send adversarial feed text to an internal service.

If operations needs these, the right route is to change the graph so that a node declares those capabilities. That way the validator sees and approves them. For example, a separate host-tier logging node, or an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` handle on an enrichment node. I'm happy to write those once the graph declares them.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;
use std::collections::HashSet;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    /// Drop every item whose id is already recorded in the `seen` store,
    /// and any repeat of an id earlier in this same batch. Order is preserved.
    ///
    /// `id` is a parser-computed digest, never feed-chosen text, so it is
    /// safe to use as a store key.
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        let mut in_batch: HashSet<String> = HashSet::new();
        let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(items.len());
        for item in items {
            if in_batch.contains(&item.id) {
                continue;
            }
            if state_read::get(&item.id).is_some() {
                in_batch.insert(item.id.clone());
                continue;
            }
            in_batch.insert(item.id.clone());
            out.push(item);
        }
        out
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

